  "planned_title": "Where Is the Nearest Star If You Shrink the Sun to a Grapefruit?",
  "spoken": "where is the nearest star if you shrink the Sun to a grapefruit. At that scale, Earth is a pinhead about fifteen meters away across a big room. The nearest star is called Proxima Centauri. a small, cool star, Proxima becomes a cherry, and that cherry is about four thousand kilometers away. Put the grapefruit in London, and the cherry is further away than Cairo.",
